and closes with the distinctive Beaufret formula

*La valeur d’une existence ne se mesure pas à la hauteur de ses réalisations, mais à la profondeur de ses racines* – “The worth of an existence is not measured by the height of its achievements, but by the depth of its roots.”

Heidegger’s conciliatory reply of 2 July 1946 reopens the dialogue and issues the renewed invitations to the Hütte that inaugurate the Todtnauberg seminars of 1946-47 and the Beaufret–Heidegger correspondence 1945-1969. 

